	(text "Seal-in latch, ngspice checked at hFE 80: stays off at power-up even with reset held, reset closes it, a 50 us contact bounce rides through,\nloop open drops it in about 100 us, re-closing the loop does nothing, a reset held through a loop cycle does nothing, a new press works 5 ms after release.\nRUN 7 V. UVLO and EN_A each take RUN through their own diode (block 10), so a fault on either pin cannot drive RUN. UVLO 3.8 V; needs about 4.8 V on RUN_B rising. Loses VCTL, RUN drops, UVLO drops: bank opens.\nLoop 6 mA, wetting for a control-rated NC contact. No 12 V on the connector without a series R. GND between loop out and return, and between return and reset: a short there opens the loop or does nothing.\nBrake resistor NC thermostat: wire it in series in the loop harness, no board parts.\nButton HB2-BS545, 22 mm mushroom, twist release, 1NC + 1NO, 660 V AC 10 A, control-rated only: NC in this loop, NO to the Pi (block 9). RUN also enables bank A (block 7) and SPARE_SW (block 8)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 284.48 240 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "29eddbb7-cd23-5e0a-9abd-744a2d80e443")
	)
	(text "3. Braking clamp: 56.8 V on, 55.8 V off, 57.5 V worst case, into the HS25"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 262 0)
		(effects
