	)
	(text "Ahead of the E-stop: motors off, compute stays up. Soft start in block 5a, BRK_PG on R.C keeps the brick off until its input is up.\n-Vout is tied to GND here: the robot has one ground, P-. RS+ and RS- tied at the pins, Trim open. Input caps at the pins; the EMC filter is left out.\n150 W at 12 V, 89 %: 18 W at full load, about 6 W at 50 W. Derating starts near 30 C at 20 LFM: fit a heatsink on the baseplate, in the Z 67 strip, see REV_B_PARTS. 12.7 mm tall: keep clear of the fan gap.\nINA228 addresses: L arm 0x40, R arm 0x41, waist 0x42, aux 0x43, L leg 0x44, R leg 0x45, 12 V 0x46, SPARE_SW 0x47, MID 0x48. Powered by the Pi's 3.3 V; Pi pull-ups on I2C."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 404 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "03b9bbb9-d78a-5b09-8554-34ce334557a3")
	)
	(text "5a. Brick soft start (ahead of the E-stop switch)"
