	(text "Same controller as the bank, so one part family. -2 retries on its own: a compute fault does not need a BMS cycle. UVLO on VIN, OVLO low: on whenever the pack is.\nPower-limit start, no dV/dt network: 70 W limit (Rs 5 mOhm, same equation as U1), about 1.3 A at full pack. 4.4 uF plus the brick's own input caps (not published) charges in under 1 ms at 20 uF.\nTimer 47 nF: 2.2 ms typ, 1.5-3.8 ms. Limit 9.7-12.3 A clears the worst brick draw, 4.7 A at 36 V. Brick input capacitance is unpublished: about 40 uF is the most the minimum timer covers, so measure one brick.\nFault check: 87 W is 1.6 A for up to 3.8 ms, against 12 A at 10 ms on the datasheet SOA. Q7 is the linear FET for that reason.\nCompute is on whenever the BMS is on. Loss at 3 A: 0.05 W shunt, 0.03 W FET."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 240 488 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b7415be3-2eb7-52ea-bf04-def665e3d999")
	)
	(text "6. Limb outputs: terminal pair, 1 mOhm shunt, INA228. Fuses inline in the pigtails."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 645 22 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9cc26f1d-aca2-579e-9f4f-1eabb091618c")
	)
