	(text "Absorber (B1): a fast breaker trip leaves the pack lead's current with nowhere to go. The diode\nlets BAT dump it into 47 uF, so a 200 A, 1 uH lead (20 mJ) charges it about 7 V, plus 6 V\nacross a 30 mOhm ESR at 200 A: about 70 V peak. Polymer, ESR 30 mOhm or less. Measure the lead\nand scope a 60 A stop. 100k bleeds it. The cap charges through the diode when the BMS closes:\n47 uF, 0.07 J, check the BMS takes it.\nF1, 1 uF, BAV19W and SMAJ15A (M14, M6, M7): a shorted U2 puts the pack on VCTL; the TVS clamps\nunder the 40 V parts and F1 opens. The BAV19W keeps C5 from back-driving U2 if BAT collapses.\nRUN_A, RUN_B and FLT_A diodes (B3): a U1 pin 2-3 bridge or an EN fault can no longer drive RUN,\nso one fault loses one bank at most.\n33k on U17 VBUS (M13). 22 nF SRC to GND, TI's recommendation for U8. BAT46W (M4). 330 uF on\n+12V: spare-output shorts and servo back-feed (M9) land in it and the compute loads."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 150 552 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
